      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Building off what Jamie said, yea, it depends on the arm length. Sure, proportionsin general are a big thing, but its mostly the lengthof your arms that determines if you can reach the ground or not. Basically, if you have impossibly long arms, you'll go through the floor really fast and everything will look microscopic. If your arms are super short or just not proportional to your legs, you can only go so far. This is all IPD scaling, and the farther your farthest wrist bone is from your descriptor viewpoint, the more the IPD scales. I hope this clears any confusion. tl;dr, Make your arms a bit longer.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
