      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "You can kind of work around this for now by tweaking your user height in the Settings menu, and using SteamVR tools like Playspace Mover or Advanced Settings to correct your vertical offset to match your standing height. Proportions can vary dramatically between avatars, so there probably isn't a single setting that'll work for everything. For example, I'm over 6'2 but my in-game height is set to 4'7, which would usually place my viewpoint around half a meter higher than my avatar's height (smol). I use SteamVR Advanced Settings to then match my viewpoint to my avatar's (and my floor to the ground), but my arms extend a little further than my avatar's arms when outstretched as a result.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
